# Plan §7b, computed initialization through a callable formal (FABLE-OPUS-RECEIVER-CONTRACT-20260924-139): f holds the
# occurrence of seven, so `i: f` -- named where a value is consumed, it runs with no arguments -- and `j: f()` both give
# its result, typed by the formal's contract (seven: an int).  i 7, j 7: w returns 77.  (Bare, the assignment's check
# typed f as the formal itself, a Structure: "incompatible type"; called, not at all: "unknown type".)  Native: a method
# with a callable formal is outside the walkable subset.  Success 7; any other value 64.
fn: seven () int
    return: 7
end: seven
fn: w (seven: f) int
    int: i
    i: f
    int: j
    j: f()
    return: i * 10 + j
end: w
int: r 0
r: w(seven)
int: ok 64
if: r = 77
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
